  Here are a few more favorites of mine :

  (a) get an amulet of life saving to avoid supid endings.
  (b) be extra careful when    
        (1) satiated
        (2) around ponds 
  (c) when you see a cockatrice :
        keep throwing arrrows or something from far or use
        those wimpy wands on hand like wand of striking.

        Having a lizard corpse does not assure safety. You
        can turn to stone immediately.

  (d) If you are playing on a machine with load, watch out
      for the delay in moves.
  
  (e) When hit points are low, climb back into previous level
      and recover them.

  (f) when hit points are low, enter a room with preferably
      one door and close it.  Stay far from that door (some 
      monsters having muchies can open doors and come at ya).
          

   (g) Using count is a safe way since the count stops as soon
      as you are hit by a monster. Keeping that "." pressed is 
      dangerous.


   (h) enter a shop and let the shopkeeper block the door (don't 
       align with him).  Then count till you recover your hit points.

   (i) when about to die,  remember to pray. 


   (j) when a monster is chasing take him around a few blocks to 
       recover hit points.  

   (k) If there are any acid blobs or floating eyes, lead them on 
       so that they block your way in a corridor.  REcover your
       hit points and then kill them.


   (l) If you have a wand of sleep, let a monster follow you into a
       blind alley and put him to sleep. Then recover your hit points.

    (m) Keep a few good things to throw and weakn a monster before you
        take him him directly.


